post_install() {
	cat <<'EOF'
sp12-camera-hal: the cameras through the IPU7 hardware ISP appear as
"Surface Front Camera ISP" and "Surface Rear Camera ISP" (v4l2loopback,
fed on demand by v4l2-relayd). To start them now:
  modprobe -r v4l2loopback; modprobe v4l2loopback
  systemctl enable --now v4l2-relayd@sp12-front.service v4l2-relayd@sp12-rear.service
then, in the desktop session: systemctl --user restart wireplumber
They start at boot once enabled. The kernel side is sp12-modules-dkms
(intel-ipu7-psys, 1.17 or later) with firmware intel/ipu/ipu7ptl_fw.bin.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
	if systemctl -q is-active v4l2-relayd@sp12-front.service 2>/dev/null ||
	   systemctl -q is-active v4l2-relayd@sp12-rear.service 2>/dev/null; then
		systemctl try-restart v4l2-relayd@sp12-front.service v4l2-relayd@sp12-rear.service
	fi
}

pre_remove() {
	systemctl disable --now v4l2-relayd@sp12-front.service v4l2-relayd@sp12-rear.service 2>/dev/null || true
}
